summary:
  The helper adds segments to a list without looking whether they are there.

history:
  The player ends a list at the first segment it cannot open. A list
  that names a segment the writer has not finished, or one it never wrote,
  ends the listener's buffer there.

target:
  package/contents/ui/tsslide.sh

find:
      while [ "$n" -le "$upto" ] && [ -s "$dir/seg-$n.ts" ]; do n=$((n + 1)); done

replace:
      while [ "$n" -le "$upto" ]; do n=$((n + 1)); done

expect:
  Killed by tests/test_tsslide.py::test_grow_does_not_step_over_a_gap.
